{"id":"tkjpeg.1","n":"tkjpeg","s":"1","src":{"r":{"pkg":"perl-Tk","ver":"804.035-8.el9","repo":"AppStream","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/AppStream/x86_64/os/Packages/p/perl-Tk-804.035-8.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/tkjpeg.1.gz","sha256":"0b714f0bd80798fe14e1831d6c8b024200ae8e454e33c6a7c5880b23609fa509","date":"2024-03-13","origin":"Tk4.003"}},"nopt":{"r":0},"desc":"simple JPEG viewer using perl/Tk","r":[["NAME","<p>tkjpeg - simple JPEG viewer using perl/Tk</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<pre>  tkjpeg imagefile.jpg\n</pre>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>Very simplistic image viewer that loads JPEG image, (well actually anything for which Photo has a handler) and puts it into a Label for display.</p> <p>It tries to find a fullcolour visual to use if display is deeper than 8-bit. (On 8-bit it uses a 4/4/4 palette.)</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>Nick Ing-Simmons &lt;nick@ing-simmons.net&gt;</p>"]]}